WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.763
An f-string lets us combine text and values in a
readable way We place the variable

00:00:05.789 --> 00:00:12.099
or expression inside braces and Python inserts its
value into the message In

00:00:12.125 --> 00:00:18.180
the example a patient name age and temperature are
combined into labeled output The

00:00:18.207 --> 00:00:23.878
temperature is also formatted to one decimal place
Run the example and then change

00:00:23.904 --> 00:00:29.784
the formatting to two decimal places so you can see
the difference F-strings

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:35.692
are especially useful in analytics because the label
value unit and formatting can travel together

00:00:36.629 --> 00:00:41.734
That makes results easier to interpret and reduces
the chance that someone will misunderstand what

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:42.944
a number represents
